WEBVTT

00:04.292 --> 00:05.209
This was halloween

00:05.250 --> 00:07.417
and this is me dressed up as

00:07.459 --> 00:09.042
a future dentist.

00:09.083 --> 00:11.042
So as a first grader, I just wrote,

00:11.083 --> 00:14.292
I know learning is important
because I wanted to help

00:14.334 --> 00:16.501
my dad and let my dad be rich.

00:18.083 --> 00:20.459
What drew me to dentistry,
my dad had his

00:20.501 --> 00:21.876
wisdom teeth extracted.

00:22.250 --> 00:24.334
A couple days later, something was wrong.

00:24.375 --> 00:26.959
He suffered a pretty bad infection

00:27.000 --> 00:28.209
that had actually spread.

00:28.250 --> 00:31.083
He actually became paralyzed
for three months.

00:31.125 --> 00:33.542
That piqued my interest in dentistry.

00:34.751 --> 00:37.709
2015 is when I had the opportunity

00:37.751 --> 00:40.459
to start my own practice in this space right here.

00:40.501 --> 00:42.417
I had no business knowledge, no training,

00:42.459 --> 00:44.417
we were just kind of stepping over one another

00:44.459 --> 00:46.542
and just bursting at the seams.

00:46.876 --> 00:49.834
And that's when I started dreaming a little bit bigger.

00:50.125 --> 00:51.918
And that gave me the confidence to

00:51.959 --> 00:54.167
take that leap of faith to expand.

00:56.626 --> 00:57.751
Hi, good to see you.

00:57.792 --> 00:59.209
Staff: Thank you
Thank you

01:00.417 --> 01:01.918
Take a seat here.

01:01.959 --> 01:03.709
Patient: I’m going to tell you I've been flossing every day,

01:03.751 --> 01:04.501
Patient: but I haven't.

01:05.834 --> 01:07.709
The cornerstone of our practice is about

01:07.751 --> 01:10.542
the relationship that we build with the patients.

01:10.584 --> 01:13.792
We really wanted to make sure they just feel at home.

01:15.000 --> 01:17.083
Yeah, I met my wife in dental school.

01:17.125 --> 01:20.709
It was never our plan to practice together.

01:20.751 --> 01:23.501
But after some time, it just made sense having

01:23.542 --> 01:26.083
Grace's pediatric practice on the first floor

01:26.125 --> 01:28.792
and my general practice upstairs.

01:30.167 --> 01:33.417
Before Lassie, Grace's purse and my backpack

01:33.459 --> 01:35.125
would just be filled with papers,

01:35.167 --> 01:37.751
we'd just be drowning in a sea of paperwork.

01:37.959 --> 01:40.459
After seeing a patient, insurance companies would

01:40.501 --> 01:43.542
mail us a paper check four to five weeks later.

01:43.584 --> 01:47.334
I was dreading having to post and manually enter

01:47.375 --> 01:48.417
hundreds of patients

01:48.459 --> 01:50.083
and thousands of procedure codes

01:50.125 --> 01:53.834
After you start staring at that piece of paper for hours,

01:53.876 --> 01:56.250
you would almost become like delirious.

01:56.751 --> 01:59.375
Lassie has been a game changer for us.

01:59.417 --> 02:02.334
Personally, it saves over a hundred hours

02:02.375 --> 02:05.918
of manual data entry time and admin time a month.

02:05.959 --> 02:08.584
It's really accelerated cash flow and now

02:08.626 --> 02:10.125
in less than a week, the money is

02:10.167 --> 02:12.334
directly deposited into my bank account.

02:12.375 --> 02:15.125
And so ...es us up to really focus on patient experience,

02:15.167 --> 02:16.959
but also growth opportunities.

02:21.125 --> 02:23.584
Because of Lassie, it's created a margin of time

02:23.626 --> 02:26.083
for my family and for me personally.

02:26.125 --> 02:28.501
And so that's allowed me to coach

02:28.542 --> 02:29.959
my kids' sports teams

02:30.250 --> 02:32.709
and to attend their practices and games.

02:33.417 --> 02:35.209
You know, I think early in my career,

02:35.250 --> 02:38.000
success was more about individual achievement.

02:38.042 --> 02:41.876
It was ... material maybe, about career, about wealth.

02:41.918 --> 02:45.042
And I realized success is about service.

02:45.334 --> 02:48.292
It's about relationships. It's about family.

02:48.334 --> 02:50.292
So that's what success means to me.
